# Where oracle_gen.go comes from. It is generated, never edited: the proof
# repository extracts its verified checkers from Rocq to MiniML JSON
# (coq/goextract/ExtractGo.v) and gogen translates the JSON to Go.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/test.yml, job "Go oracle provenance") checks out NC_REPO
# at NC_COMMIT, extracts the JSON in ROCQ_IMAGE, runs gogen with GOGEN_ARGS, and
# requires the JSON and the Go to have exactly these hashes, and the Go to equal
# oracle_gen.go byte for byte. To move to a new proof commit, run
# internal/oracle/regenerate.sh <commit> and update NC_COMMIT and both hashes.
# GOGEN_ARGS must match the proof repository's coq/goextract/Makefile (gen).
NC_REPO=blackwell-systems/normalization-confluence
NC_COMMIT=60df67f321e35f4ce7b35ef6938a882b7d83334b
ROCQ_IMAGE=rocq/rocq-prover:9.3@sha256:c357e8864f80359db21725ea8371347a75a1cb439545b47219d7ad5683ba1782
GOGEN_ARGS=-pkg oracle -allow-unary-file allow-unary.txt
JSON_SHA256=1192dc794d4ed84b37210fbabdc8d0e9d356cdce00148bc5c2cf20b08fd084f4
GO_SHA256=20dc6ebc481be5e17f0c894593239e5129616f94f940e97c58ee5b052b92741b
